12 participants; behavioural accuracy 48.9-96.7%

=== behaviour vs decoding ===
  behaviour ~ within-subject 3-class (correct only) n=12   rho +0.63 p 0.029    r +0.34 p 0.285
  behaviour ~ within-subject 3-class (all trials) n=12   rho +0.65 p 0.023    r +0.50 p 0.096
  behaviour ~ LOSO 3-class (correct only)        n=12   rho +0.21 p 0.519    r +0.20 p 0.536
  behaviour ~ within-subject lateral             n=12   rho +0.44 p 0.154    r +0.46 p 0.131
  behaviour ~ LOSO lateral                       n=12   rho +0.62 p 0.032    r +0.56 p 0.056

  10 comparisons, none corrected. smallest p = 0.023, Bonferroni threshold 0.05/10 = 0.0050 -> none survives

=== consistency between the two decoding problems ===
  (not independent: the lateral problem reuses 720 of the same trials)
  lateral within ~ 3-class within (all trials)   n=12   rho +0.74 p 0.006    r +0.69 p 0.014
  lateral within ~ 3-class within (correct only) n=12   rho +0.74 p 0.006    r +0.62 p 0.031

